ying to get the minesweepers to  allow us to shrink their turrets  essentially and put guns fake guns and  you know so there was a lot of there was  a lot of legwork and a lot of in  pre-production there was a lot of a lot  of legwork on how do we build the East  more how do we on a 21-foot tide how do  we how do we even start to build it  we've got a four-hour window to put the  steel plates in and then we have to  build it up and by the end of the day we  have to get onto the decking of that  session and then the next thing we have  to do it all again and so until we sort  of slowly step out to sea so it was by  far most logistical challenging film a  lot of people probably would give up  because those battles we have to try and  get this even the mold built in heavy  weather or persuade Dutch ships to come  over and with their historic ships and  we have to change them you know a lot of  people would immediately go to the  digital aspect but we knew we'd sort of  ruin the film if we did that so you know  it was a lot of legwork and holding fast  as I and it honestly it took every film  we've done before to be able to achieve  this because we knew we could do it it  was about keeping people with us to help  us you know the French authorities that  the mayor had to help the the city had  to agree to let us rebuild the mall we  had to keep our modder on the in the  inland docks you know and that was  before we even got to the small ships  and landed a real Spitfire on the beach  so you know so it was I'm very proud of  that film but when I watch it it was I  remember every day and so so that was  pre-production then we started filming  and then it's then you're on this it's a  big freight train coming down the line  and we have to always open the set and  then I have to move on to figure out  that the next day's work so Chris will  always say to me what are you still  doing you need to get onto tomorrow and  and so we always work ahead but you know  as usual we're working in more than one  country so it's a lot of travelling  involved so you're running three art  departments and you've got to keep  everyone moving  [Music]
 

